  "title": "No Reversible Gray Representative in a Specified Orbit of a Length-34 Quaternary Legendre Pair",
  "batch_label": "72",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "disproved",
  "scope": "Let n=34; map digits 0,1,2,3 to 1,i,-1,-i; take A=2202202000022020222202000220200020 and B=1133303133112311101113211331303331; define (c_r X)_j=X_{j-r} and (d_k X)_j=X_{j k^{-1}} on Z_34; and let Gamma_34(A,B) be exactly the set of s^e(alpha c_r d_k(A^epsilon), beta c_t d_k(B^epsilon)) with alpha,beta in {1,i,-1,-i}, r,t in Z_34, k in Z_34^times, and epsilon,e in {0,1}. Then Gamma_34(A,B) contains no ordered pair whose four Gray rows all satisfy x_j=x_{-j} for every j in Z_34. This is only a conclusion about the displayed frozen Gamma_34, not about any larger qLP equivalence relation or other length-34 qLPs.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
